  "summary": "Draw Component (Cart Variation) – PWA Kit Component",
  "description": "As a Developer, I want to build the cart drawer as a reusable PWA Kit component, so that it can be triggered from any surface on the site and render the correct state based on the current basket contents.\n\nThis is a PWA Kit component story — it covers the cart drawer container, header states, open/close behaviour, and responsive layout. It does not cover accessibility since this is just a variation of the drawer component.\n\nIt does not cover the components that render within the drawer — each has its own dedicated story. The drawer is the container component for all other cart stories and is a dependency for;\n\n- [SFCC-270](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-270) \n- [SFCC-274](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-274) \n- [SFCC-316](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-316) \n- [SFCC-318](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-318) \n- [SFCC-404](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-404) \n\nThe open and close animation for the cart drawer is defined in [https://zimmermann-handover-ja2o39l78-song-ddp-anz.vercel.app/#templates%2Fmain](https://zimmermann-handover-ja2o39l78-song-ddp-anz.vercel.app/#templates%2Fmain)\n\n*Full Cart:*\n\n![\"image-20260908-034058.png\"](image-20260908-034058.png)\n\n\n\n*Empty Cart:* \n\n![\"image-20260908-034026.png\"](image-20260908-034026.png)",
